I'm assuming you're referring to Xconq, which over the past six years
has gone through many many versions, more than I imagined when I first
put it out on the net!  The latest "official" version is 5.5.1a,
available from ftp.uu.net and elsewhere.  There is also a version
6.0 running around, and I'm working on a 7.0 as well, just to add to
the confusion. :-)  Since many of these versions are drastically different
from each other, it is important to specify which version you're using.
It would be even better if you knew whether this was a locally modified
version, since people sometimes reports bugs in code that I've never
even heard of before!

It would also be helpful to supply at least the command line, and a
copy of the game period file.

Feel free to send me the details, although I can't promise a solution,
since all my pre-version-7 code is packed away and I've forgotten much
about how it works.  There is a mailing list xconq@uunet.uu.net that may
prove helpful also.

